
  <sn><md>### What a literal character is

A literal character matches itself. Letters, digits, spaces, and most punctuation are literals, so the pattern `hello` matches the exact text "hello" and nothing else. The engine reads the pattern left to right and looks for those characters in that exact order.

```
Pattern:  cat
Text:     "The cat sat on a concatenated scatter."
Matches:  "cat" in "cat", "concatenated", and "scatter"
```

Notice that `cat` matches inside larger words too. A regex doesn't know about words unless you tell it to (with word boundaries like `\b`, which come later).
</md></sn>
